flowchart LR
  accTitle: Four stages of the GraSP control path
  accDescr: GraSP links four stages. Memory-conditioned retrieval proposes skills from semantic relevance and episodic experience. DAG compilation creates a typed executable graph. Verified execution checks node preconditions and postconditions and repairs failures locally. Confidence-based routing sends unreliable retrieval to reactive fallback.
  Q[Task and current state] --> R[1. Memory-conditioned retrieval]
  M[(Episodic experience)] --> R
  L[(Typed skill library)] --> R
  R --> C[2. DAG compilation]
  C --> X[3. Verified execution and local repair]
  X --> T[4. Confidence-based routing]
  T -->|Reliable structured path| X
  T -->|Low retrieval confidence| F[ReAct fallback]
  classDef source fill:#EAF4FB,stroke:#1A4A8A,color:#1C1C1E
  classDef process fill:#F4F4F4,stroke:#888888,color:#1C1C1E
  classDef output fill:#EEF7EE,stroke:#27AE60,color:#1C1C1E
  classDef caution fill:#FEF9E7,stroke:#F39C12,color:#1C1C1E
  class Q,M,L source
  class R,C,X,T process
  class F caution
